./docs/WORK-ORDERS-archive.md:132:- [x] **BW-10 (MERGED Batch B) — PDF export broken: `soffice not found`.** ROOT CAUSE = STALE SANDBOX IMAGE (env, not code). `libreoffice-impress` IS in deploy/sandbox/Dockerfile:53-59 (W-22 `141dc9c`), but the deployed `disco-sandbox:base` (gVisor VM201 / local) predates that layer / never rebuilt (memory: prod base-image rebuild still open). The capability gate `_deck_pdf_capable` (deck_editor.py:102-106) only checks BACKEND TYPE, not whether soffice exists → gate passes, box spins, `soffice: not found` → RuntimeError → 422. FIX: (1) OPS — rebuild+redeploy disco-sandbox:base from the updated Dockerfile on every backend; (2) HARDEN — gate on a real `command -v soffice` probe (pattern at _pptx_render.py:1311-1324) so a stale image reports "PDF unavailable in this image" + hides the button instead of a dead failure.
./docs/WORK-ORDERS-archive.md:133:- [x] **BW-11 (MERGED Batch B) — PDF-export error ejects user to a raw backend error page.** ROOT CAUSE (frontend): exports are plain CROSS-ORIGIN `<a href download>` (DeckExportBar.tsx:104-114) to the agent-server (different origin) → `download` ignored → click = top-level navigation → on non-2xx the route's JSON error body (deck_editor.py:288-300/334-337) is rendered as a page, leaving the SPA. FIX: replace the anchor with `fetch()` → `response.ok` ? Blob object-URL synthetic download : parse `{reason,message}` + in-app toast (reuse DeckEditorPane patchNotice). Also makes BW-10's failure an in-app message.
./docs/WORK-ORDERS-archive.md:134:- [x] **BW-12 (MERGED Batch B) — HTML export DUPLICATE slides (two title + two outline).** ROOT CAUSE (shared w/ BW-13): `lower_deck` splits overflowing slides into `_cont` continuations (_deck_schema.py:996-1004), created as `type=f"{aslide.type}_cont"` SUPPOSED to re-infer as bullets — but `_infer_layout` does `slide.type.removesuffix("_cont")` (:406), so `title_cont`→`title` / `section_header_cont`→`section_header` → the continuation renders the SAME title layout + SAME title text = duplicate title/outline pages. `_fit_text` (:290-348) over-aggressively splits ordinary decks. FIX: force `_cont` slides to `bullets` (don't let removesuffix map them back to title/section/closing) + blank/relabel the duplicated title ("… (cont.)"); recalibrate _fit_text so normal decks don't over-split.
./docs/WORK-ORDERS-archive.md:135:- [x] **BW-13 (MERGED Batch B) — Slide-count mismatch (13 exported vs 10 in editor).** ROOT CAUSE (same as BW-12): the export path `lower_deck` SPLITS overflow into `_cont` slides (10→13), but the editor map `lower_deck_for_editor` iterates `authored.slides` 1:1 with NO split (_deck_schema.py:1104) → editor shows 10. FIX: make `lower_deck_for_editor` apply the SAME overflow split (or both share ONE slide-expansion pass) so editor count == exported count. (Fix BW-12+BW-13 together.)
./docs/WORK-ORDERS-archive.md:136:- [x] **BW-14 (MERGED Batch B) — Editor theme change has no visual effect.** ROOT CAUSE (frontend): the Theme picker state is LOCAL to DeckExportBar (useState `disco-light` :60) and only builds the export `<a>` hrefs; DeckEditorPane fetches the preview via `getDeckRenderHtml(cid,base)` with NO template arg (:55,:100) though the API+route fully support `template` (api/agent.ts:209-227, deck_editor.py:188-238). So switching theme re-points the download link but the iframe keeps the authored theme. FIX: lift `templateId` to DeckEditorPane (pass value+onChange to DeckExportBar), thread into `getDeckRenderHtml(cid,base,templateId)`, + a useEffect re-fetching render HTML on templateId change (guard with the renderSeqRef token :43,99-103).
