./basis-of-design.md:32:2. **The Agent** — a Manus-class autonomous worker. A user states a goal; the system produces a visible plan, executes it as a tool-using loop inside a secure sandbox (browsing, running code, writing files, building and previewing deliverables), shows the work live, and yields a finished artifact the user owns.
./basis-of-design.md:119:**Decision:** Local open-weight models via Ollama/llama.cpp are primary. OpenRouter is the overflow path for hard planning/synthesis and high-precision verification. Routing is **capability-based** behind an `LLMRouter` abstraction.
./basis-of-design.md:152:│  • Owns the sandbox lifecycle for its conversation                 │
./basis-of-design.md:248:- **ConversationErrorEvent / status events** — lifecycle signals (e.g., max-iterations reached, stuck).
./basis-of-design.md:307:- **Confirmation policy:** `ConfirmRisky` (gate on risk threshold; confirm-on-UNKNOWN), with the plan-preview gate up front (§13.2).
./basis-of-design.md:364:- **Deploy/preview:** start a dev server / produce a preview URL for built artifacts (§8.2, Labs-style).
./basis-of-design.md:385:- **Sandbox instance** — a running microVM created from a spec, with lifecycle (create / start / stop / destroy) and user-scoping.
./basis-of-design.md:417:### 12.2 Step lifecycle (one iteration)
./basis-of-design.md:435:- **First pass:** the agent *creates* the action but does not execute it; status → WAITING_FOR_CONFIRMATION; the loop stops and surfaces the proposed action (and, up front for a whole plan, the plan-preview gate, §13.2).
./basis-of-design.md:437:This is the same machinery for (a) the upfront plan-preview gate and (b) per-action gating of risky steps (§17).
./basis-of-design.md:472:- Default surface = timeline; the live desktop is **one click away** in the Inspector. We explicitly avoid the "black box with no live preview" failure that drew criticism of Perplexity's Personal Computer — an intermediate/live view is always available.
./basis-of-design.md:474:### 13.2 The plan-preview gate (highest-leverage feature)
./basis-of-design.md:493:- **Deep Research report view:** sidebar-pinned table of contents, document navigation, export to PDF/Markdown/shareable HTML.
./basis-of-design.md:494:- **Labs/builder view (Agent deliverables):** multi-pane — **Apps** (live iframe preview of generated HTML/CSS/JS), **Tasks** (workflow visualizer), **Assets** (downloadable artifacts), **Sources**. Edits are **scoped** ("change the secondary chart to a scatter plot" modifies only that scope via version history + visual diffs, never regenerating the whole artifact and destroying manual tweaks).
./basis-of-design.md:516:Citation faithfulness is a **pipeline problem, not a prompt** — strong models still leave a meaningful fraction of claims unsupported on their own. We build a verification stage; we do not rely on instructions.
./basis-of-design.md:521:3. **Automatic verification:** split the answer into atomic claims; run a per-claim **NLI/entailment check** (premise = retrieved passage; hypothesis = claim) using a compact cross-encoder (§12 model roles; e.g., a DeBERTa-v3-large-MNLI-class model, ~300M params — *not* an LLM).
./basis-of-design.md:523:5. **Surface honestly:** unsupported/weak claims and broken sources are shown as such in the UI (§13.3), never hidden.
./basis-of-design.md:526:Generation + first-pass NLI verification run **fully local** (the cross-encoder is trivial next to the LLMs). A frontier "judge" via OpenRouter is reserved for **periodic eval sampling** (§20), not the live path — keeping per-answer latency and cost local while still measuring quality honestly.
./basis-of-design.md:547:Overflow to OpenRouter **only** on: low local confidence, repeated tool errors / stuck recovery, the hardest planning/synthesis steps, or high-precision verification. Every overflow decision is logged (§20). The local/overflow threshold is a **tunable policy**, not hardcoded.
./basis-of-design.md:550:A Deep Research run ≈ 20–40 model calls; route only the 5–10 hardest to a frontier model → on the order of low-single-digit to ~$18 per run at mid-frontier rates, near-zero marginal cost for the local majority. **The plan-preview gate (§13.2) cuts this 30–50%** by trimming exploration before it runs. Quantization guidance: Q4_K_M/Q5_K_M for the 30–70B driver; secondary models tolerate Q4_K_S/IQ4_XS.
./basis-of-design.md:603:- **Metrics:** per-run token/cost (local vs overflow), iteration counts, stuck-detection fires, condensation events, retrieval latency and source counts, citation-verification pass rates.
./basis-of-design.md:628:- **Cost:** dominated by overflow; bounded by the plan-preview gate (§13.2, §15.4) and local-first routing.
./basis-of-design.md:670:- **Live agent-working UI:** plan-preview gate, three-tier disclosure, Activity Feed + confidence gradient, **Inspector** (noVNC PIP, smart diffs, scratchpad), **Steering Wheel** redirect, and the **kill switch** (§13.2, §13.4, §13.6).
./basis-of-design.md:676:- **Deep Research mode** (long-horizon loop, ToC report view, export) (§8.1, §13.5).
./basis-of-design.md:707:| R9 | **Cost runaway** on overflow | Low | Med | Plan-preview gate (30–50% cut), local-first routing, per-run cost logging and budget alerts (§15, §18, §21). |
